/tmp/arxiv2405.VcmENj/main_arXiv_V3.tex:762:\subsection{The decidable tractability criterion}
/tmp/arxiv2405.VcmENj/main_arXiv_V3.tex:764:We are now ready to provide a decidable reformulation of the tractability criterion from Theorem~\ref{sellingmainthm_general} avoiding all infinite-domain CSP jargon.
/tmp/arxiv2405.VcmENj/main_arXiv_V3.tex:767:Either $\CSP(\bA)$ is NP-complete, or one of the following cases holds, in all which $\CSP(\bA)$ is in P. 
