STEP 0 has narrowed the viable route. The paper’s main theorem is a P/NP-complete dichotomy, and its explicit Section 6.4 hard template lacks a constructive distributional-hardness reduction, so the prior “plant any orientation” hypothesis is not enough for Track A. I’m now checking a native Track B route licensed by Sections 6.2–6.3: clique-orientation constraints preserved by the minority (edgewise XOR) operation, with Gaussian elimination as the disclosed mechanical algorithm and a short coboundary/switching shortcut as the intended insight.
